  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>At Le Brusc, in Six-Fours-les-Plages, Bruscain Paddle rents paddleboards (paddle or motorised) and inflatable kayaks and gives beginner lessons, for two months a year, in July and August. It also offers equipment delivery at Le Brusc (corniche des Îles).</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>According to its website, welcoming dogs is the company's specialty: you can paddle or kayak with your dog. For dog outings, the website mentions suitable paddleboards, life jackets for dogs, a waterproof bag, a bowl, treats and small toys. Rentals include free cold drinks, the waterproof bag and a phone pouch. The Provence Méditerranée tourist office listing ticks "pets allowed" and mentions lessons that can be individual, in a group or with pets.</p>

      <h2>Booking and published prices</h2>
      <p>Booking and questions by phone, text or call, on 06 67 30 20 49 (the company's number, given by the website as the easiest way to book). Prices from the "Nos prix paddle et kayak" page: paddleboard 18 € per hour, 24 € for 2 hours, 33 € for a half day; paddleboard lessons 45 € per hour, including a "dog" lesson at the same price; kayak 20 € per hour, 35 € for 2 hours, 40 € for a half day, 50 € for a full day; sunset outing 21 €; motorised water scooter 35 € for 30 minutes, 60 € per hour; group discounts are available. The Provence Méditerranée tourist office shows other amounts (paddleboard 18 € per hour, kayak 14 € per hour): the company website's prices are the ones used here. The website also offers equipment delivery at Le Brusc, corniche des Îles, for rentals by the day, the week or longer.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: call before coming to arrange the outing, especially if it's your dog's first time on a paddleboard.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>The company says it serves Six-Fours-les-Plages, Le Brusc and the surrounding area; the tourist office describes it as a mobile activity, with a postal address on Traverse du Gaou and delivery at the corniche des Îles. Ask by phone where your outing starts and whether your dog can go aboard with its life jacket, especially a large dog.</p>
